# Auth windows — ask here first

The operator uses **two browser sessions**. The default/personal session has **no** access to work AWS or Grafana. A login that auto-opens a window lands in the wrong profile and fails.

## Before any of these

- `aws sso login` (profile `mvr` or otherwise)
- Grafana / `gcx login` / Cloud OAuth
- Any CLI that opens a browser for auth

**Stop and prompt in this chat.** Do not run the command yet. Say what needs auth and wait for an explicit go-ahead.

## After they say go

Use **device-code** (or pasteable URL + code), never a silent default-browser launch:

```text
aws sso login --profile mvr --use-device-code
```

Put the verification URL and code in the chat so they can paste it into the **work** session.

Do not retry the no-flag `aws sso login` that calls `oidc…/authorize` with `redirect_uri=127.0.0.1`.
